<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33479" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pallēnē</span></b> ,
		ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παλλήνη</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a peninsula and town of Macedonia</i>, <i>on the Thermaic Gulf</i>, <i>also
				called</i> Phlegra, <i>where the battle between
				the gods and the giants took place</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 10,
				17, § 36</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 15,
				356</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 2, 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Herc. Fur. 979</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pallēnaeus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Pallene</i>, <i><span class="en">Luc. 7,
			150</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">triumphi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 4, 2, 56</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pallēnensis</span></b> ,
			e, adj., <i>Pallenian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					44, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">isthmus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					4, 10, 17, § 36</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
